  "priorExpiration": "2008-12-28",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Alc 402.01 Certification and Licensure Expiration Dates and Filing Deadlines for Renewals.\n\n(a) All certifications and licenses shall automatically expire 2 years from the date of issuance.\n\n(b) Certifications and licenses shall be renewed on or before the date the certification or license is to expire.\n\nSource. #9199, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 7-1-08, EXPIRED: 12-28-08\n\nNew. #9356, eff 1-9-09; ss by #10273, eff 2-20-13; ss by #12548, eff 7-1-18; ss by #14045, eff 10-7-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/alc100-500.html"
